:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"><br>Note that from ﬁrst year occupancy (psi1), colonization (g(t)) and extinction probabilities (e(t)),</font></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">occupancy in future years (yt+1) can be calculated with the recursive equation:</font></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">y(t+1) = y(t)*(1-epsilon (t) + (1-y(t))*g(t)   </font></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"></font> </div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">Then I would get different answers for each year.</font></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"></font> </div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">So I guess what I&#39;m asking is whether the unconditional occupancy rates estimated for years 2 and years 3 (for example <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">best@projected</a>) are based on the above equation or not?  In other words is the intercept value for occupancy from the &quot;best&quot; model, the expected occupancy in year 1 and then year 2 and year 3 are estimated from the extinction colonization rates?</font></div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"></font> </div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"></font> </div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">Thanks,</font></div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\"></font> </div><div style=\"font:13px/normal arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:0px;white-space:normal;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:normal;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">\r\n<font color=\"#3333ff\">Robin</font></div></span><div st